<h2>1. How to add a new Property to be managed by the GUI</h2>
<p>Assuming you have already one new field in one of the GUI screens
and you require to add a new property to be managed by the GUI, you must
add the property in several places. Here you will find the guideline to
do it.</p>
<h3>1.1 Adding new property to Carmen XML Parser</h3>
<ol>
	<li>
	<p>XMLTokens</p>
	<ol>
		<li>
		<p>Select the file "carmen.io.networks.xml.XMLTokens"</p>
		</li>
		<li>
		<p>Add one descriptor for the new property (if required)</p>
		</li>
		<li>
		<p>Save the file</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>XMLReader</p>
	<ol>
		<li>
		<p>Select the file "carmen.io.networks.xml.XMLReader"</p>
		</li>
		<li>Add the reader into one of the appropriated sub-elements of
		the reader</li>
		<li>
		<p>Save the file</p>
		</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>
	<p>XMLWriter</p>
	<ol>
		<li>
		<p>Select the file "carmen.io.networks.xml.XMLWriter"</p>
		</li>
		<li>Add the writer into one of the appropriated sub-elements of
		the writer</li>
		<li>Save the file</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
</ol>
<h3>1.2 Adding new property to ProbNode</h3>
<p>Properties in the ProbNode are stored in a HashMap, so adding a
new attribute/property is done automatically by the NodeWrapper class
and the Parser.</p>
<h3>1.3 Adding new property to NodeWrapper</h3>
<ol>
	<li>Select the file "carmen.gui.networks.NodeWrapper.java"</li>
	<li>Add the appropriated setPropertyXXX in the method
	"setProperties(...)"</li>
	<li>Add the appropriated getPropertyXXX call in the method
	"getProperties()"</li>
	<li>Add the method "getPropertyXXX" to retrieve the information
	from ProbNode equivalent property</li>
	<li>Add the method "setPropertyXXX" to store the information to
	ProbNode equivalent property</li>
</ol>
<h3>1.4 Adding new property to NodeProperties</h3>
<ol>
	<li>&nbsp;Select the file
	"carmen.gui.networks.NodeProperties.java"</li>
	<li>Add an attribute (the new property) into the attribute's
	section of the file.
	<ol>
		<li>Do not forget to add a proper comment to identify the meaning
		of the new attribute</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>Add the initial value in the Constructor Method</li>
	<li>Add the appropriated getter and setter methods after the last
	get/set method of the file
	<ol>
		<li>If you are using Eclipse, then you can use the "Generate
		getter/setter" facility (remember, right click on the new attribute,
		then Source, then Generate...).</li>
		<li>Do not forget to add a proper comment to identify the meaning
		of the new attribute</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>Add to the "equals" method</li>
	<li>Add to the "toString" method</li>
	<li>If the attribute you are adding belongs to a specific network,
	then add a "remove" action in the method "adaptToClipboard"</li>
</ol>
<h3>1.5 Modifying the appropriated Test Cases</h3>
<p>When you have completed the previous steps, you must verify the
following test cases in the &nbsp;test package:</p>
<ul>
	<li>carmen.gui.networks.NodePropertiesTest.java</li>
	<li>carmen.gui.networks.NodeWrapperTest.java</li>
	<li>carmen.io.networks.XMLReaderTest.java</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
